QuestGuidance.Register("en",434,{
[13857]="7000D3CD\n1\tCollect crawler remains (total: 6)\tCrawlers can be found throughout Fasach-larran. Tasgall has asked you collect remains from the crawlers of Fasach-larran so he may create bait to lure out Bangrath and Murragrath.\n2\tBring crawler remains to Tasgall\tTasgall's camp-site is north of Aughaire and south-east of Nád Nathair. You have collected the remains of several crawlers from Fasach-larran, and should bring them now to Tasgall.\n",
[13858]="7004D70F\n1\tFind Karazgar's agents and their cargo at Esgaroth-of-old\tEsgaroth-of-old can be found to the east of Eryn Lasgalen on the banks of the Long Lake. Thranduil has learned that Karazgar's agents have returned to Esgaroth-of-old, and he seeks to put an end to the Weeping Warrior's plot against the North.\n2\tBurn the remains of slain cold-drakelings in Esgaroth-of-old (total: 18)\tSlain drakelings can be found near the bones of Smaug in Esgaroth-of-old. You have discovered the smuggled drakelings laid bare in Esgaroth-of-old as a means to incite the ire of the Herald of Winter.\n3\tPatrol Esgaroth-of-old in search of the Weeping Warrior\tKarazgar might be found somewhere in Esgaroth-of-old. You should search for Karazgar in Esgaroth-of-old. He might be found near the bones of Smaug.\n4\tFollow the path of slain Men along the old bridge\tThe path of slain Men can be found along the broken bridge to Esgaroth-of-old. You have not found any sign of the Weeping Warrior, but you discovered a path of slain Men leading down the old bridge of Esgaroth. You should see where it leads.\n5\tExamine the dying cold-drake\tThe cold-drake can be found amid the bones of Smaug in Esgaroth-of-old. You have not found Karazgar, but a dying cold-drake stares towards the bones of Smaug from the old bridge. You should examine the cold-drake.\n6\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. A cold-drake has delivered a chilling threat against the people of the North. You should warn King Thorin III.\n",
[13859]="70030F57\n1\tTalk to Walnoth at the Cliving Mead Hall dungeon\tWalnoth awaits your return at the dungeon entrance below the Cliving mead hall. Ides has informed you that Walnoth has requested to speak with you regarding the outcome of your investigation.\n2\tTalk to Eldora in the dungeon\tEldora is being held in a cell in the Cliving dungeon, under the Mead Hall. Walnoth has asked you to inform Eldora of her confirmed innocence and that she is being set free.\n3\tTalk to Walnoth about Eldora's request\tWalnoth waits at the dungeon below the Cliving Mead Hall. Eldora has asked you to convince Walnoth to grant healing and treatment to the soldier who was in her care.\n",
[13860]="70030F5B\n1\tTalk to Walnoth at the Cliving Mead Hall dungeon\tWalnoth awaits your return at the dungeon entrance below the Cliving Mead Hall. Ides has informed you that Walnoth has requested to speak with you regarding the outcome of your investigation.\n2\tTalk to Wigfugol in the dungeon\tWigfugol is being held in a cell in the Cliving dungeon, under the Mead Hall. Walnoth has asked you to inform Wigfugol of his confirmed innocence and that he is being set free.\n3\tTalk to Walnoth about Wigfugol's request\tWalnoth waits at the dungeon below the Cliving Mead Hall. Wigfugol has requested that Walnoth gather a company of soldiers to retake the Norcrofts farmland lost to their Orcs.\n",
[13861]="70030F46\n1\tTalk to Walnoth at the Cliving Mead Hall dungeon\tWalnoth awaits your return at the dungeon entrance below the Cliving Mead Hall. Ides has informed you that Walnoth has requested to speak with you regarding the outcome of your investigation.\n2\tTalk to Swithorne in the dungeon\tSwithorne is being held in a cell in the Cliving dungeon, under the Mead Hall. Walnoth has asked you to inform Swithorne of his confirmed innocence and that he is being set free.\n3\tTalk to Walnoth about Swithorne's request\tWalnoth waits at the dungeon below the Cliving Mead Hall. Swithorne has asked you to convince Walnoth erect a memorial statue in Cliving to honour the fallen soldiers.\n",
[13862]="70064EF4\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Treasure Bugan barter currency allowance.\n",
[13863]="70072A7D\n1\tDefeat Pakhán-gebar, Servant of Stone\tExplore the caves of Hurum Kâna for signs of Bârlat and his brigands.\n2\tDefeat the Council of Thieves\tYou hear rough voices and sharp tongues echoing through the musty cave. Steel yourself for the dangers to come and press further into Hurum Kâna.\n3\tDefeat Bârlat the Bold\tYou hear a loud and boisterous voice echo through the caves. Bârlat must be close. Pursue him!\n",
[13864]="70072A7E\n1\tDefeat Pakhán-gebar, Servant of Stone\tExplore the caves of Hurum Kâna for signs of Bârlat and his brigands.\n2\tDefeat the Council of Thieves\tYou hear rough voices and sharp tongues echoing through the musty cave. Steel yourself for the dangers to come and press further into Hurum Kâna.\n3\tDefeat Bârlat the Bold\tYou hear a loud and boisterous voice echo through the caves. Bârlat must be close. Pursue him!\n",
[13865]="70072A80\n1\tDefeat Pakhán-gebar, Servant of Stone\tExplore the caves of Hurum Kâna for signs of Bârlat and his brigands.\n2\tDefeat the Council of Thieves\tYou hear rough voices and sharp tongues echoing through the musty cave. Steel yourself for the dangers to come and press further into Hurum Kâna.\n3\tDefeat Bârlat the Bold\tYou hear a loud and boisterous voice echo through the caves. Bârlat must be close. Pursue him!\n",
[13866]="70072A7F\n1\tDefeat Pakhán-gebar, Servant of Stone\tExplore the caves of Hurum Kâna for signs of Bârlat and his brigands.\n2\tDefeat the Council of Thieves\tYou hear rough voices and sharp tongues echoing through the musty cave. Steel yourself for the dangers to come and press further into Hurum Kâna.\n3\tDefeat Bârlat the Bold\tYou hear a loud and boisterous voice echo through the caves. Bârlat must be close. Pursue him!\n",
[13867]="700269AD\n1\tTalk to Halthor Goldeneye\tYou should speak with Halthor Goldeneye to receive your treasure-hunter's picks.\n",
[13868]="70044E3B\n1\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin, in Dunland\tTheodore Gorse is in the small settlement of Avardin, on the western side of Dunland. Bingo has asked you to see what Theodore thinks about beginning the journey north in the settlement of Galtrev.\n2\tTalk to Bingo in Galtrev, in Dunland\tBingo is down the hill west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev. Bingo has agreed to meet you and his other companions in Galtrev, the large settlement in the middle of Dunland.\n3\tTalk to Haley Meadowsweet in Galtrev\tHaley Meadowsweet is down the hill west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev. Theodore seems to be missing, and Bingo wants to know if Haley knows where he has gone.\n4\tSearch the upper eastern plateau in Galtrev\030Search the skirmish camp in Galtrev\030Search the farmland outside of Galtrev\030Search the south-west entrance of Galtrev\tTheodore Gorse is missing, and Haley Meadowsweet wants you to search various locations in Galtrev for her absent student.\n5\tTalk to Haley Meadowsweet in Galtrev\tHaley Meadowsweet is down the hill to the west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev. You were unable to find Theodore in Galtrev, and should return to Haley to see if she found him.\n6\tTalk to Humfrey Rumming in Galtrev\tHumfrey Rumming is on the hill west of the eastern gate of Galtrev. Theodore is missing, and so is the Rothstone. Does Humfrey Rumming know something about these disappearances?\n7\tTalk to Bingo in Galtrev\tBingo is down the hill west of the eastern entrance to Galtrev. Theodore has apparently gone to a place of great danger with the Rothstone, and Bingo wants to speak with you before it is too late to rescue the foolish Treasure Seeker.\n8\tTalk to Bingo in Galtrev and travel with him to Draigoch's Lair\tBingo is on the hill west of the eastern gate of Galtrev. Bingo has resolved to follow Theodore to the lair of the dragon in Thrór's Coomb, and is waiting for you to speak with him.\n9\tTalk to Theodore Gorse outside Lhanuch\tTheodore Gorse is outside the settlement of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.\n10\tTalk to Haley Meadowsweet outside Lhanuch\tHaley Meadowsweet is outside the settlement of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.\n11\tTalk to Bingo outside Lhanuch\tBingo Boffin is outside the settlement of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.\n",
[13869]="70072EC1\n1\tLocate the double-locked chest\tLocate the whereabouts of the treasure that has been stashed within this cavern.\n2\tGather keys for double-locked chest (total: 2)\tGather keys spread throughout the cavern.\n3\tReturn to the double-locked chest\tReturn to the double-locked chest.\n4\tDefeat the ambush\tSurvive the ambush in the cavern\n5\tDefeat Ruhíshi the Bounteous\t\n6\tUnlock the double-locked chest and gather the goods\tWith the ambush defeated, unlock the double-locked chest and gather the goods.\n",
[13870]="70008138\n1\tUse Stolen goods (total: 9999)\030Use Stolen goods\tStolen crates from Trestlebridge lie scattered throughout the large Orc encampment north-east of Trestlebridge. You should search the creates and collect treasure.\n2\tCollect all the missing pages from the Founder's Book\tThe pages of the Founders Book have been scattered by the Orcs near Trestlebridge. You should collect all of the missing pages from the Founder's Book.\n3\tTalk to Marla Shelton\030Collect The Founder's Book\tMarla Shelton is back in Trestlebridge. You have found the Founder's Book and should bring it back to Marla Shelton.\n",
[13871]="700096FE\n1\tTalk to Sid Waring\tSid Waring's camp is encamped with Helechír. Helechír has asked you to warn a man named Sid Waring of the possibility of attack by tomb-robbers.\n2\tBring stolen relics to Helechír\030Collect stolen relics (total: 4)\tSome of the stolen relics are on an island next to Sid Waring's camp; others were carried to another island camp to the south in Men Erain. Helechír is at Sid Waring's camp. Sid Waring has been wounded, but he remains hale enough to tell you he was attacked by men he knew out of Ost Forod. He mentioned a leader called Brychan the Bold and asked you to recover the relics that were stolen from the ruin he was hired to protect.\n",
[13872]="7000EF95\n1\tPresent the Jewel of Ice to Rikitsa in Sûri-kylä\tRikitsa is at Sûri-kylä, well north of Pynti-peldot. Esko has asked you to bring the Jewel of Ice to Rikitsa at the Council.\n",
[13873]="700490FB\n1\tFind an Orc who might know what Krassa-phûrsa is seeking\tAn Orc under the command of Dulgabêth might be found somewhere in Dor Amarth, perhaps spying on those who travel on the road south-west of Lûghash. You should find an Orc who might know what Krassa-phûrsa is seeking.\n2\tFind an Orc who might know where Krassa-phûrsa has gone\tAn Orc under the command of Dulgabêth might be found somewhere in Dor Amarth, perhaps spying on those who travel on the road south of Lûghash. You should find an Orc who might know what Krassa-phûrsa is seeking.\n3\tLook Around for signs of Krassa-phûrsa at her last known location\tKrassa-phûrsa's last known location can be found in Dor Amarth, south-east of Lûghash. You should go to Krassa-phûrsa's last known location.\n4\tFind an Uruk who might know more about Krassa-phûrsa's task\tAn Uruk that might have seen Krassa-phûrsa can be found in Dor Amarth, south-east of Lûghash, off the main road through Dor Amarth. You should find an Uruk who might know if Krassa-phûrsa has retrieved what she is seeking.\n5\tFind an Uruk who might know more about Krassa-phûrsa's task\tAn Uruk that might have seen Krassa-phûrsa can be found in Dor Amarth, south-east of Lûghash, off the main road through Dor Amarth. You should find an Uruk who might know where Krassa-phûrsa has gone.\n6\tSeek out and confront Krassa-phûrsa\tKrassa-phûrsa can be found in Dor Amarth, on the foothills of the Ered Lithui. You should seek out and confront Krassa-phûrsa.\n7\tThink about what to do next\tDefeated Krassa-phûrsa.\n8\tTalk to Lômazar\tLômazar is located in the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth. You should speak to Lômazar.\n",
[13874]="70015E35\n1\tBring the relics to Ladenthir at Echad Eregion\030Collect relics (total: 15)\tHalf-orcs can be found in Barad Morlas, south-west of Echad Eregion. Ladenthir is at Echad Eregion, north-east of Barad Morlas. Ladenthir believes that the half-orcs have uncovered many Elf-relics at Barad Morlas and asks that you defeat them and recover the relics.\n",
[13875]="70001799\n1\tInvestigate Amon Amrûn\tAmon Amrûn is in the eastern Fields of Fornost. Colbert the Mad wants you to investigate Amon Amrûn, for he claimed there was a great deal of treasure there, but he was afraid to claim it.\n2\tSearch for signs of looters at Amon Amrûn\tAmon Amrûn is in the eastern Fields of Fornost. The shades of Amon Amrûn seem to be disturbed because their ancient tomb has been robbed.\n3\tSpeak with the person who followed you here\tSomeone is watching you from a hill just south of Amon Amrûn. You should confront the person who followed you here.\n",
[13876]="70025A3D\n1\tSearch within the store-room\tBarad Tharsír is across the Baranduin, south-east of the colossus. Daerol asked you to return to Barad Tharsír, enter the store-room, and discover what the robbers are doing there.\n2\tTalk to Daerol\tDaerol is at the colossus, north-west of Barad Tharsír. Daerol will want to know that the robbers were excavating the ruins, and the carts were full of nothing but dirt and rubble.\n",
[13877]="70003400\n1\tBring the ancient journal to Tobold Leafcutter\030Search the Northern Barrow for an ancient chest\tYou may find a chest resting at the Northern Barrow, the northernmost barrow of the Barrow-downs. Tobold Leafcutter waits for you between the Old Forest and Barrow-downs. Tobold Leafcutter has asked you to search the Northern Barrow for more lore. He hopes that lore from the Men of Cardolan may have survived the long years since the Great Plague in a chest. If you find such lore, you should bring it to Tobold.\n",
[13878]="7002BFE0\n1\tCollect Treasure-stores from Helstor (total: 6)\tTreasure-stores can be found in a cave within Helstor, north of Etheburg. Céola asked you to go to recover the stolen treasures from the brigands of the Brown Lands.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south of Helstor. You should bring the recovered relics to Céola.\n",
[13879]="7005AB17\n1\tCollect plundered dwarf treasure (total: 6)\tPlundered dwarf treasure can be found inside the giant-hold of Thyrstáth. You should collect plundered dwarf treasures.\n2\tCall Hórin and talk to him\tUse the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side. You should talk to Hórin.\n",
[13880]="7004AB96\n1\tSearch rubble for lesser artifacts (total: 12)\tMany lesser artifacts can be found scattered across Dor Amarth. You should find any lesser artifacts that you can.\n",
[13881]="7002EEFA\n1\tCollect Wulfrad's coffer\030Collect Wulfrad's seal\030Collect Wulfrad's ring from Wulfrad's treasure box\tValuables once belonging to Thane Wulfrad, Béortnoth's father, might still remain in the ruins of the Mead Hall of Thornhope. Máthild asked you to find valuables once belonging to Thane Wulfrad so that she might present them to the new Thane, Béortnoth.\n2\tTalk to Máthild outside Thornhope\tMáthild is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope. You should bring the items you found to Máthild.\n3\tBring the items you found to Béortnoth outside of Thornhope\tThane Béortnoth is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope. Máthild asked you to bring the items you collected to Thane Béortnoth.\n",
[13882]="70071633\n1\tCollect ancient treasures (total: 10)\tThe Tombs of Khâb Ishil house many historical treasures from the kingdom of Nísaka. You should collect ancient treasures at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil.\n2\tTalk to Malêrti\tYou have collected many treasures from the Tombs of Khâb Ishil. You should return to Malêrti at the Dawn-warden.\n",
[13883]="700450FB\n1\tEnter the cellar in Bâr Nadhron\tThe time has come to enter the cellar in Bâr Nadhron, in the Beacon Hills, and pay the ransom for Glánhar's sons.\n2\tReturn to Gondrad\tYou should return to Gondrad and tell him all that took place in the cellar at Bâr Nadhron.\n",
[13884]="70051542\n1\tYou should wear a costume and collect treats from housing neighbourhood doormats. To help participation in this event, be sure to place the doormat you received from Begonia Grubb on your own house! More doormats can be obtained from Mogo Bracegirdle.\t\n2\tReturn to Begonia Grubb\tBegonia Grubb can be found in Wistmead, by the Party tree, and in the town centre of all housing neighbourhoods. Return to Begonia Grubb and tell her about the treats you collected while in costume.\n",
[13885]="700655A3\n1\tMark cullable trees (total: 5)\tTordiril has asked your assistance in marking trees for cutting. Trees to be marked can be found in northern Lower Lebennin.\n2\tReturn to Tordiril\tYou should let Tordiril know that you have marked trees in the forest for culling. Tordiril is at Zarsatrâd.\n",
[13886]="7002C759\n1\tDestroy Orc weapon-stores (total: 12)\tOrc-weapons have been amassed in their large camp to the south of Thinglad. You should destroy the weapon-stores of the Orcs before these tools can be used to harm the trees or creatures of the forest.\n2\tReturn to Renfaer\tRenfaer is at his scouting location near the centre of Thinglad. You should return to Renfaer.\n",
[13887]="7004A8D0\n1\tPatrol Torech Ungol and inspect the tunnel into Shelob's lair\tTorech Ungol can be found to the south-west of Cirith Ungol in Lhingris. Legolas has grown concerned by the continued tremors beneath Lhingris and fears that Shelob shall soon venture forth from her lair.\n2\tTalk to Legolas outside Cirith Ungol\tLegolas can be found beside the road to Cirith Ungol. You have discovered the tunnel into Torech Ungol unblocked and open to Lhingris. You should return to Legolas.\n",
[13888]="70000C39\n1\tTalk to Frideric the Elder\tHead down the Greenway from Trestlebridge and then east along the east-west road. Go to Ost Guruth and talk to Frideric the Elder.\n",
})
